diff --git a/native-runtime/nvn/README.md b/native-runtime/nvn/README.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/native-runtime/nvn/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,280 @@
+# Native NVN resource ownership
+
+`Resources` owns logical device, pool and buffer objects keyed by aligned guest
+integer addresses. It owns real Vulkan devices, buffer allocations and aliased
+views through `graphics/VulkanDevice`. No host pointer is written into guest
+state. Typed descriptions keep compatibility layouts and numeric flag decoding
+outside the component. No Core, kernel/process, Maxwell or service objects enter
+this interface.
+
+The initial supported pool mode is GPU cached with CPU cached or CPU no access.
+Virtual/physical pools and other cache modes fail explicitly. Backing storage
+and pool size require 4096-byte alignment; size is bounded to 16 MiB. Initial
+upload uses at most sixteen 1 MiB guest-read callbacks. Every explicit transfer
+is bounded to 1 MiB. Buffer views can have arbitrary in-range byte offsets and
+may alias the same pool. Distinct pools with overlapping guest backing are
+rejected because independent Vulkan allocations could diverge.
+
+CPU map returns the guest storage address (plus buffer offset), never a mapped
+host pointer. CPU-no-access pools reject map/flush/invalidate. Explicit flush
+reads guest bytes into temporary storage before updating/flushing Vulkan memory;
+a read failure leaves Vulkan bytes unchanged. Invalidate downloads/invalidate
+Vulkan bytes then invokes the guest write callback. A write failure is explicit
+and can retain partial guest effects according to the callback contract. CPU
+writes are not automatically coherent with Vulkan memory; callers must flush.
+
+`PoolGpuAddress`/`BufferGpuAddress` return real Vulkan buffer device addresses.
+`ResolveGpuAddress` resolves only a live owning pool and checked range.
+`Backend`, `View` and `Binding` borrow native objects for shader/command work;
+callers must complete GPU use before mutating or destroying them. Calls,
+callbacks and destruction are confined to the owner thread. Callbacks must be
+bounded, synchronous and non-reentrant. Live buffers block pool destruction;
+live pools block device destruction. Final owner teardown frees all resources.
+
+Build this directory standalone using the existing MSVC/Vulkan headers. The test
+submits a real `vkCmdCopyBuffer`, waits on a fence for at most five seconds and
+reads 64 copied bytes through guest-memory invalidation. It also checks real BDA,
+view aliasing, callback faults/partial writes, invalid ranges/modes/alignment,
+backing alias rejection, lifetime, key reuse and wrong-thread access. CTest has a
+30-second timeout. This is resource/GPU-copy evidence, not game rendering.
+
+Provenance: locally authored implementation, no LASRecomp code copied. The
+architectural reference was inspected at LASRecomp revision
+`99f783df21f60f48d512b95dd6536cb1ab48c2af` (MIT), `runtime/nvn/objects.c`.
+That title uses different builder offsets/default `0x9`, host pointers stored in
+guest objects and GPU-address-equals-CPU-address assumptions; none was adopted.
+It contains no verified public memory-pool flag enum. Numeric MK8D flag decoding
+therefore remains outside this typed API pending separately verified constants.
+No actual multi-block MK8D DeviceInitialize/MemoryPoolInitialize interception,
+presentation, draw submission, automatic guest coherence or standalone service
+closure is claimed by this component.
+
+## Bounded offscreen draw
+
+`draw.h` accepts caller-owned SPIR-V and an explicit scalar descriptor plan for
+set 0: uniform buffer ranges and combined RGBA8 2D sampled textures. It accepts
+location 0 float4 vertices with explicit stride, nonindexed or uint16/uint32
+indices, triangle lists/strips, bounded viewport/scissor and disabled/source-alpha
+blending. Target and texture dimensions are at most 2048; draw counts are at most
+1,048,576. Indices are checked against the vertex view before submission. No
+descriptor layout, shader input, texture contents or game arguments are inferred.
+
+Each call owns its temporary Vulkan image, upload/readback buffers, nearest/clamp
+samplers, descriptors, pipeline, command resources and fence. Texture uploads use
+explicit image transitions. A real draw is followed by image readback and a
+transfer-to-host barrier; the normal path waits up to five seconds for completion
+before returning owned RGBA8 bytes. Exception cleanup after a successful submit
+waits for device idle before destruction, so driver failure cleanup is not a
+hard real-time operation. Borrowed Resources buffers/device must remain alive,
+and all prior external queue uses must be complete. The API is owner-thread only.
+
+SPIR-V must already be valid Vulkan SPIR-V. Preflight checks structure, version,
+single main entry/stage, Logical GLSL450 model, enabled capability subset,
+32-bit scalar types, scalar UBO/combined nonarray 2D descriptor types and the
+explicit binding plan. Push constants, storage buffers, descriptor arrays,
+specialization constants, extensions and unimplemented capabilities fail
+explicitly. This targeted preflight does not replace a complete SPIR-V validator.
+Uniform ranges conservatively must cover reflected fixed scalar/vector/array/struct block
+members using explicit Offset/ArrayStride metadata. Unknown matrix/runtime
+layouts reject rather than allowing a shader to read beyond its bound range.
+This is the component's conservative rule, not a universal Vulkan requirement
+for unused block tails. Captured logical bytes must remain exact; no invented
+padding is used to satisfy it. A smaller binding requires separately verified
+active-access coverage before relaxing this rule.
+
+`native_nvn_draw_test` uses Sirit-authored fixture shaders: vertex location 0
+float4 and a fragment shader multiplying one UBO by samples from two textures.
+It checks known pixels for draw/draw-indexed, both index widths, topology,
+scissor and source-alpha blending, and rejects invalid metadata/state/indices.
+Those authored fixtures demonstrate component behavior only. They are not an
+actual MK8D draw, resource capture or evidence of native title rendering.
+
+Core Matrix/Shader/ImageQuery/SampledBuffer capabilities are accepted. Optional
+ImageGatherExtended is accepted only when `VulkanHandles` reports that the
+physical feature was queried and enabled on the actual device. Declaring a core
+capability does not widen the typed descriptor subset (buffer textures remain
+unsupported). The pure preflight entry point allows testing the disabled-feature
+case; GPU entry points always use the actual backend feature value.
+
+`CheckProgramPipeline` and `native_nvn_pipeline_check` create/destroy a real
+graphics pipeline using caller-supplied modules and an explicit per-stage binding
+plan. The CLI's `vertex:ubo:N`/`fragment:ubo:N`/`fragment:sampler:N` arguments must
+come from matching reflection evidence. It returns before command allocation or
+submission, binds no resource contents and produces no image. Pipeline acceptance
+does not establish actual game resource correctness or native title rendering.
+
+## Persistent frames and typed state
+
+`FrameImages` owns persistent images, views and samplers. `FrameEncoder` snapshots
+programs, draw state, fixture textures and ordered UBO versions, then preflights
+the complete supported graph. Device leases and vertex/index buffer leases
+protect lifetime and overlapping transfers while recording or in flight.
+Committed layouts/content change only after completed GPU work; failed recording
+cannot publish a layout. StoreDiscard invalidates previous content. Load and
+sampling require established content. Exact compatible backing aliases are
+interned; partial/incompatible ranges reject. No virtual-key-only image identity
+or buffer/image coherence conversion is inferred.
+
+The semantic state API supports this explicit subset:
+
+|State|Supported contract|
+|---|---|
+|Blend|Independent RGB/alpha Zero, One, SourceAlpha, OneMinusSourceAlpha or SourceColor factors; ADD; RGBA write mask|
+|Vertex input|One active location 0 float2/3/4, checked aligned byte offset/stride and reflected floating shader input; divisor 0; checked uint16/uint32 index/base-vertex arithmetic|
+|Raster/viewport|Fill; no cull or back cull; explicit CW/CCW; positive or explicitly inverted Y; depth/stencil/write/bias/discard disabled|
+|Sampled images|R8Unorm, Rg8Unorm, Rgba8Unorm, Rgba8Srgb, A2B10G10R10Unorm; exactly one mip, layer and sample; typed view component mappings|
+|Sampler|Independent nearest/linear min/mag and mip filtering, repeat/clamp-edge per axis, finite ordered LOD bounds/bias; normalized coordinates, comparison off, anisotropy1|
+|Targets|Linear Rgba8Unorm or A2B10G10R10Unorm, identity attachment swizzle; explicit Load/Clear/Discard and Store/Discard|
+
+`DrawDescription::blend_state` is explicit. Combining it with a non-disabled
+legacy blend preset rejects. `Blend::SourceAlpha` keeps its historical RGB
+SourceAlpha/OneMinusSourceAlpha and alpha One/OneMinusSourceAlpha semantics.
+Selecting explicit alpha SourceAlpha is distinct and tested. The old
+`DrawOffscreen` fixture adapter keeps its 2048 target limit and existing output;
+persistent typed images use actual device/format limits instead.
+
+`SamplerDescription::state` selects semantic state while legacy fields remain at
+their defaults. Non-default/conflicting legacy sampler fields reject. Captured
+LOD bounds may be retained with the exactly-one-mip view; this does not invent
+missing mip contents. Image-view swizzles affect sampling without rewriting
+source bytes. The new `ReadbackImage` returns format, dimensions, row-byte count
+and raw format bytes. Legacy `Readback` accepts only linear RGBA8, preventing
+R8/RG8/sRGB bytes from being silently called RGBA8 output.
+
+`VulkanDevice::GetCapabilities` reports effective enabled core API version,
+actual image/viewport limits, viewport bounds and sampler bias limit. Negative
+viewport height is enabled here only when the effective API is at least 1.1;
+physical-device support alone does not enable it. InvertY maps logical y,height
+to Vulkan y+height,-height and does not secretly flip front-face state again.
+Image usages, linear filtering and target blending are checked against actual
+format properties. Image allocation has a configurable 256 MiB default budget;
+coherent host staging is required. Unsupported format/state requests reject.
+Depth/stencil, instancing, anisotropy/comparison, multiple
+mips/layers/samples and feedback remain unsupported.
+
+`native_nvn_state_test` uses independent CPU blend/UNORM, sRGB transfer and
+framebuffer geometry equations. Before the packed extension below, the initial
+typed step passed 49 draws, 199680 pixel checks and 59
+rejections, including 5120-wide R8, float3 poisoned padding, independent alpha
+blending, all channel masks, R/R/R/1 and R/R/R/G swizzles, linear/repeat sampling,
+both windings/orientations and unaligned native buffer views. Rejected alignment
+cases prove frame counters/content unchanged. Existing resource/draw/frame
+fixtures remain passing. Vulkan validation layers are not enabled by this test
+backend; passing tests do not claim validation-layer cleanliness.
+
+This adds renderer capabilities only. Actual capture replay remains gated on
+complete shader identity/state, authoritative source/initial destination
+contents, physical aliases and inherited raster/sample/depth behavior. No clear,
+padding, missing texture or middle CPU readback/reupload may be invented to close
+those gaps. No actual-game draw, presentation or native gameplay is claimed.
+
+Scoped MSVC static analysis: isolated Release build of native_nvn_resources and
+native_nvn_state_test with /W4 /analyze /EHsc passes. Own changed units have no
+remaining diagnostic. Inherited resources.h pin initializers make_shared<uint8_t>(0)
+produce C4244 through MSVC STL templates (integer literal0 to uint8_t); disclosed
+separately, no suppression/vendor changes. Analysis logs are private under
+native-platform/frame-state-analysis-*.log. No further GPU tests were run after
+warning cleanup: removed unused/shadow locals, made existing descriptor rejection
+explicit and added defensive null-map checks; leader's sanitized build will
+repeat the four suites.
+
+
+## Packed 10-bit persistent images
+
+`ImageFormat::A2B10G10R10Unorm` supports persistent color targets and sampled
+views when the actual device reports the requested usages, blending and filter
+capabilities. It maps to `VK_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM_PACK32`: R bits 0..9,
+G 10..19, B 20..29 and A 30..31 in a little-endian 32-bit word. The mapping follows
+[Khronos format definitions](https://docs.vulkan.org/refpages/latest/refpages/source/VkFormat.html)
+and NVIDIA's [Maxwell texture schema](https://github.com/NVIDIA/open-gpu-doc/blob/9fdf5c4062007929d9f4e6cbad9c9771fe61b880/classes/3d/clb197tex.h).
+Renderer enum values remain semantic; no unchecked compatibility-API numeric
+cast selects the format.
+
+Uploads and `ReadbackImage` preserve packed words and return explicit format and
+row-byte metadata. Legacy RGBA8 `DrawResult`/`Readback` does not reinterpret or
+convert packed images. Native producer-to-sampler flow keeps the packed image
+on the GPU; there is no intermediate RGBA8 upload/readback or precision loss.
+The existing single-mip, identity-attachment-view, alias/lifetime, content-validity
+and submission-failure contracts apply unchanged.
+
+The synthetic state fixture now passes 76 draws, 306176 pixel checks and 66
+rejections on the recorded device. Packed-specific cases cover exact raw upload
+and readback, clear quantization, four non-tie alpha2 quantization cases, all 16
+channel masks with exact preserved bits on Load, source-alpha and multiplicative
+blending, nearest/linear sampling and an exact packed producer-to-packed-consumer
+chain. The chain preserves RGB integer values 77/511/839 out of 1023 and alpha
+1 out of 3, which an RGBA8 intermediate cannot preserve. RGB arithmetic accepts
+one 10-bit LSB of conversion rounding; chosen non-tie alpha values and untouched
+channels are checked exactly. Metadata extent and backing-alias failures reject.
+
+`native_nvn_packed_oracle` runs 4096 CPU packing roundtrips and checks explicit
+primary channel bit positions and UNORM quantization with zero GPU calls. All
+five resource/draw/frame/state/oracle CTests pass. Scoped MSVC `/W4 /analyze
+/EHsc` passes for the changed packed units; inherited token-initializer warnings
+are described above. Validation layers remain disabled. This is synthetic
+format evidence, not an actual capture replay or native-game rendering claim.
+
+## Native Win32 presentation (synthetic fixture)
+
+`DeviceOptions::presentation` is opt-in. `RetainPresentationWindow` creates a
+host-only retained Window/surface pin; HWND/HINSTANCE never enter guest storage.
+The existing VulkanDevice enables verified surface/swapchain and matching
+KHR/EXT maintenance1 extensions/features, creates the actual surface before
+selecting one graphics+present queue, and retains Window through surface teardown.
+Offscreen construction still requests no WSI extensions and keeps its defaults.
+A live surface blocks explicit Window destruction. Resources creation forwards
+the typed device option; existing C++ consumers require matching rebuilt headers
+and libraries when this option or Window layout changes.
+
+`Presenter` shares that device and `DrawIntoTarget`; no second renderer/device is
+created. A strict procedural fullscreen triangle needs no fabricated guest vertex
+buffer and rejects shaders with active vertex attributes. A retained
+`PresentSource` validates committed image contents, sampled usage, format and
+actual native device identity on every use. Invalidated/terminal sources reject
+before acquisition/submission. Native sources remain pinned through conversion
+completion; no CPU image readback/reupload transports frames.
+
+The first policy accepts linear-sRGB-primary RGBA8 or packed10 source, explicit
+opaque output, and a reported SDR RGBA8/BGRA8 UNORM/sRGB surface pair. sRGB
+attachments encode once; UNORM surfaces use an authored GPU encoding shader.
+Final packed10-to-SDR8 display quantization is explicit and does not alter source
+bits. Independent GPU conversion checks compare both source formats against a
+CPU sRGB equation and verify invalid retained-source rejection.
+
+Acquisition, render completion and presentation retirement are distinct states.
+Acquire semaphores and per-image render-finished semaphores are consumed before
+reuse; maintenance1 presentation fences establish safe WSI resource retirement.
+Submit fences or DeviceWaitIdle are not substituted for presentation fences.
+Close/resize/error paths retain acquired-image state, consume orphan signals and
+release acquired images or retire queued presentations. Zero/minimized extents
+pause; out-of-date/suboptimal chains recreate from fresh capabilities. A creation
+failure that retires an old swapchain does not resume using it.
+
+All first-fixture work is on the window/graphics owner thread. Fence polling
+pumps messages, but driver creation/submit/present/drain can stall; there is no
+hard five-second total-return/close guarantee. Long work is outside generated C
+and bounded metadata callbacks. Actual guest NVN presentation remains gated on
+its separate device/owner scheduling contract.
+
+`native_nvn_presentation_policy` is headless and checks retirement/error policy
+and CPU transfer-function values. `native_nvn_presentation_conversion` uses real
+Vulkan offscreen color oracles. The visible `native_nvn_presentation_fixture` is
+NOT registered in default CTest and requires `--visible`; it creates only its own
+synthetic window, exercises both GPU-produced source formats, minimize/restore,
+resize and close. Optional capture is restricted to its verified unoccluded
+physical client rectangle, with per-monitor-aware context selected before HWND
+creation. No focus forcing or changes to unrelated windows are required.
+
+Verified on the recorded AMD device: effective Vulkan 1.2, queue family 0, enabled
+VK_KHR_surface/VK_KHR_win32_surface/VK_KHR_get_surface_capabilities2/
+VK_KHR_surface_maintenance1 and VK_KHR_swapchain/VK_KHR_swapchain_maintenance1.
+Seven headless suites passed. The accepted visible run queued and retired 45
+presentations, recreated 3 swapchain generations and performed 0 source readbacks.
+Both owned-client captures show the authored red top-left quarter and gradient;
+this is bounded synthetic window evidence, not actual-game presentation or exact
+scanout/monitor color accuracy. Validation layers were not enabled. Early GDI and
+incorrectly DPI-cropped diagnostics were invalid and excluded from acceptance.
+
+Scoped MSVC W4/analyze/EHsc is clean for the changed units; inherited resource-pin
+initializer C4244 diagnostics remain separate. Rebuilt affected native_graphics,
+shader_module_check, BufferInit and Window test consumers accompany the change.
diff --git a/native-runtime/nvn/buffer_init.cpp b/native-runtime/nvn/buffer_init.cpp
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/native-runtime/nvn/buffer_init.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@
+#include "buffer_init.h"
+#include <array>
+#include <stdexcept>
+namespace native_nvn {
+namespace {
+bool Overlap(uint64_t a, uint64_t as, uint64_t b, uint64_t bs) {
+  return a <= b ? b - a < as : a - b < bs;
+}
+uint64_t Le(std::span<const std::byte> bytes) {
+  uint64_t value = 0;
+  for (size_t i = 0; i < bytes.size(); i++)
+    value |= uint64_t(bytes[i]) << (8 * i);
+  return value;
+}
+} // namespace
+BufferInitializer::BufferInitializer(Resources &resources,
+                                     BufferInitMemory memory)
+    : resources_(resources), memory_(memory),
+      owner_(std::this_thread::get_id()) {
+  if (!memory.probe || !memory.peek || !memory.read || !memory.write)
+    throw std::runtime_error("BufferInit callbacks required");
+}
+void BufferInitializer::CheckOwner() const {
+  if (owner_ != std::this_thread::get_id())
+    throw std::runtime_error("BufferInit owner thread required");
+}
+void BufferInitializer::RegisterPool(GuestAddress pool, GuestAddress device,
+                                     uint64_t size, size_t object_bytes) {
+  CheckOwner();
+  resources_.Backend(device);
+  const auto actual = resources_.ResolveGpuAddress(
+      device, resources_.PoolGpuAddress(pool), size);
+  if (actual.pool != pool || actual.offset)
+    throw std::runtime_error("Native pool association mismatch");
+  if (!pool || (pool & 7) || !size || object_bytes < 18 ||
+      object_bytes > 4096 || pools_.contains(pool))
+    throw std::runtime_error("Native pool registration invalid");
+  pools_.emplace(pool, OwnedPool{device, size, object_bytes});
+}
+void BufferInitializer::UnregisterPool(GuestAddress pool) {
+  CheckOwner();
+  if (!pools_.erase(pool))
+    throw std::runtime_error("Native pool not registered");
+}
+void BufferInitializer::Finalize(GuestAddress output) {
+  CheckOwner();
+  resources_.DestroyBuffer(output);
+}
+BufferInitResult BufferInitializer::Initialize(GuestAddress output,
+                                               GuestAddress builder) {
+  CheckOwner();
+  const BufferInitResult decline{BufferInitOutcome::Decline, 0},
+      fault{BufferInitOutcome::Fault, 0};
+  if (!output || (output & 7) || (builder & 7) || output > UINT64_MAX - 48 ||
+      builder > UINT64_MAX - 32 || Overlap(output, 48, builder, 32) ||
+      !memory_.probe(memory_.user, output, 48, true) ||
+      !memory_.probe(memory_.user, builder, 32, false))
+    return decline;
+  std::array<std::byte, 32> snapshot{};
+  if (!memory_.peek(memory_.user, builder, snapshot))
+    return decline;
+  const auto device = Le(std::span(snapshot).subspan(0, 8)),
+             pool = Le(std::span(snapshot).subspan(8, 8));
+  const auto offset = Le(std::span(snapshot).subspan(16, 8)),
+             size = Le(std::span(snapshot).subspan(24, 8));
+  const auto owner = pools_.find(pool);
+  if (owner == pools_.end() || owner->second.device != device ||
+      pool > UINT64_MAX - owner->second.object_bytes ||
+      Overlap(output, 48, pool, owner->second.object_bytes) ||
+      !memory_.probe(memory_.user, pool + 17, 1, false))
+    return decline;
+  try {
+    const auto actual = resources_.ResolveGpuAddress(
+        device, resources_.PoolGpuAddress(pool), owner->second.size);
+    if (actual.pool != pool || actual.offset)
+      return decline;
+  } catch (const std::runtime_error &) {
+    return decline;
+  }
+  bool live_output = false;
+  try {
+    resources_.Binding(output);
+    live_output = true;
+  } catch (const std::runtime_error &) {
+  }
+  try {
+    resources_.PoolGpuAddress(output);
+    live_output = true;
+  } catch (const std::runtime_error &) {
+  }
+  try {
+    resources_.Backend(output);
+    live_output = true;
+  } catch (const std::runtime_error &) {
+  }
+  if (live_output)
+    return decline;
+  std::array<std::byte, 1> flag{};
+  if (!memory_.peek(memory_.user, pool + 17, flag))
+    return decline;
+  const bool failure = (uint8_t(flag[0]) & 1) != 0;
+  if (!failure && (!size || offset > owner->second.size ||
+                   size > owner->second.size - offset))
+    return decline;
+  bool created = false;
+  if (!failure) {
+    try {
+      resources_.CreateBuffer(output, {device, pool, offset, size});
+      created = true;
+    } catch (const std::runtime_error &) {
+      return decline;
+    }
+  }
+  auto fail = [&] {
+    if (created)
+      resources_.DestroyBuffer(output);
+    return fault;
+  };
+  std::array<std::byte, 16> zero{};
+  for (auto at : {32u, 16u, 0u})
+    if (!memory_.write(memory_.user, output + at, zero))
+      return fail();
+  std::array<std::byte, 8> value{};
+  if (!memory_.read(memory_.user, builder + 8, value))
+    return fail();
+  if (Le(value) != pool)
+    return fail();
+  std::array<std::byte, 1> actual_flag{};
+  if (!memory_.read(memory_.user, pool + 17, actual_flag) ||
+      actual_flag != flag)
+    return fail();
+  if (failure)
+    return {BufferInitOutcome::Failure, 0};
+  const uint64_t expected[] = {device, pool, offset, size};
+  for (size_t i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+    if (!memory_.read(memory_.user, builder + i * 8, value) ||
+        Le(value) != expected[i])
+      return fail();
+    if (!memory_.write(memory_.user, output + 8 + i * 8, value))
+      return fail();
+  }
+  return {BufferInitOutcome::Success, 1};
+}
+} // namespace native_nvn
diff --git a/native-runtime/nvn/buffer_init.h b/native-runtime/nvn/buffer_init.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/native-runtime/nvn/buffer_init.h
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+#pragma once
+#include "resources.h"
+namespace native_nvn {
+enum class BufferInitOutcome { Decline, Success, Failure, Fault };
+struct BufferInitResult {
+  BufferInitOutcome outcome;
+  uint32_t value = 0;
+};
+struct BufferInitMemory {
+  void *user = nullptr;
+  // Pure NORMAL-owned-RAM checks/snapshots, never bus reads/fault callbacks.
+  bool (*probe)(void *, uint64_t, size_t, bool write) = nullptr;
+  bool (*peek)(void *, uint64_t, std::span<std::byte>) = nullptr;
+  bool (*read)(void *, uint64_t, std::span<std::byte>) = nullptr;
+  bool (*write)(void *, uint64_t, std::span<const std::byte>) = nullptr;
+};
+// Verified builder schema: device,pool,offset,size at +0,+8,+16,+24;
+// output is 48 bytes; pool validation byte at +17, bit0 forbids initialization.
+// No title addresses are selected here. Registration is only for native-owned
+// pools; reference objects must never be registered. Owner-thread/quiescent
+// metadata; no output alias with builder/pool object. All calls are synchronous
+// bounded metadata/view bookkeeping; they allocate no GPU storage and wait on
+// no GPU.
+class BufferInitializer {
+public:
+  BufferInitializer(Resources &, BufferInitMemory);
+  void RegisterPool(GuestAddress pool, GuestAddress device, uint64_t size,
+                    size_t object_bytes);
+  void UnregisterPool(GuestAddress pool);
+  BufferInitResult Initialize(GuestAddress output, GuestAddress builder);
+  void Finalize(GuestAddress output);
+
+private:
+  struct OwnedPool {
+    GuestAddress device;
+    uint64_t size;
+    size_t object_bytes;
+  };
+  Resources &resources_;
+  BufferInitMemory memory_;
+  std::map<GuestAddress, OwnedPool> pools_;
+  std::thread::id owner_;
+  void CheckOwner() const;
+};
+} // namespace native_nvn
