@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+# Native Maxwell-to-SPIR-V bridge
+
+`Snapshot` owns a checked graphics shader environment. `TranslatePair` calls the existing shader-only flow CFG, Maxwell translation and SPIR-V emitter using native-owned pools; it creates no Maxwell3D, GPU command processor, Core::System or guest-memory objects. The standalone target links the frozen current-host shader_recompiler/common/fmt/Sirit/Boost libraries; no video_core library or public video_core header is used.
+
+Input format is explicitly pinned to little-endian 64-bit suyu `yuzucach` version18. This reader currently accepts only the first pipeline's exactly-two VertexB/Fragment environments. It bounds the file at64MiB, shader code at1MiB+8, metadata counts at65536, checks instruction ranges/alignment, enum values, duplicate metadata, and duplicate SPH agreement. It does not validate or iterate the remaining pipeline records/key suffix. Unknown format/stage, truncated/range-invalid inputs and missing required cbuf/texture metadata fail. Optional cbuf replacements return absent when the recorded map has no entry, matching the shader contract. Compute/tessellation/geometry/dual-vertex and image/texel-buffer resource plans are unsupported.
+
+Translation uses an explicit conservative SPIR-V1.0 profile, float generic attributes/fragment outputs, triangle topology and carried vertex varying/legacy-store state. These are declared assumptions, not decoded raster/vertex state from the cache key. Translation success does not prove complete graphics semantics, pipeline validity, descriptor contents or rendered equivalence. Resource/interface output describes the emitted modules under this profile.
+
+`native_shader_probe owned-vulkan.bin output-directory` reads an owned local capture and writes vertex.spv, fragment.spv and resource-plan.json only to the requested private output directory. Game shader/cache bytes are not embedded in source. The probe tests malformed/truncated/version/count/stage cases and missing metadata before translating the actual pair.
+
+`native_shader_module_check vertex.spv fragment.spv` uses the existing native graphics resource device and system loader to create/destroy both VkShaderModules. This is driver module acceptance, not SPIR-V formal validation, pipeline creation or a draw. It submits no command buffers. Run GPU-facing checks only under the root's replay coordination.
+
+First observed MK8 pair: vertex input location0 float4; vertex output Position and locations1/2 float4; fragment input locations1/2 float4, color output0 float4. Descriptor set0 has vertex cbuf3 at binding0, fragment cbuf3 at binding1, and two fragment combined2D image samplers at bindings2/3, sourced from cbuf2 offsets0x20/0x28. No push constants. The cache supplies compile-time handle/type words, not complete cbuf3 bytes, texels, sampler states, vertex data, viewport/scissor, blend/depth or render-target contents. A correct real native draw requires those runtime resources and state; a fabricated uniform/texture fixture would not establish MK8 rendering correctness.
+
+The parser follows the pinned serialized schema documented in src/video_core/shader_environment.cpp without including that implementation. Existing shader sources carry their GPL/SPDX notices; retain those licenses and frozen-library provenance. No LAS shader translator or shaderc dependency was imported.
+
+## Bounded all-record catalog and exact matching
+
+`CacheIndex::Read` consumes the complete version18 cache, rather than just the legacy first-pair prefix. It supports all serialized stages, including compute workgroups/shared memory and geometry passthrough masks. Bounds:64MiB input,4096 pipeline records,8192 environments,6 graphics stages,1MiB+8 per code span,65536 entries per metadata map. Graphics stage ordering and nonzero pipeline-key stage slots must agree; compute records must contain one compute stage and matching key metadata. The pinned Win64 serialized key sizes are1056 graphics/24 compute, verified by a private source-layout probe. The native library still includes no VideoCommon/GPU/Core headers.
+
+Each entry exposes complete-code SHA256, instruction-only SHA256, normalized environment-metadata SHA256, exact raw pipeline key and its SHA256, record/stage identity, code bounds, SPH, geometry mask, workgroup and recorded cbuf/texture/replacement maps. Normalization sorts maps; it does not change values. Pipeline key provenance is separate from shader-environment identity.
+
+`MatchComplete` requires explicit stage and code layout (`SnapshotCode` includes graphics SPH; `InstructionsOnly` excludes its80 bytes). It requires equal full length, SHA256 and actual bytes. No prefix matching, padding, stage fallback, shortest/longest selection, first-pair fallback or default resource metadata occurs. Missing matches and distinct environment-metadata ambiguity throw. Byte-identical code with identical complete environment metadata reports all aliases; their pipeline keys may still differ. A canonical alias does not select actual raster state or a pipeline.
+
+Version18 serializes Surface::PixelFormat raw ordinals0..111. The existing Shader::TexturePixelFormat enumeration lacks ten ETC/EAC entries beginning at95. Catalog/hash/index preserve raw ordinals exactly; queried `ReadTexturePixelFormat` explicitly rejects95..111 at the native shader boundary rather than casting them into a different semantic format. Query logs show which formats an actual translation needed. Catalog success is not blanket translation capability. Required missing cbuf/type/format reads still fail; no metadata is invented.
+
+Tools:
+
+- `native_shader_index index owned-cache.bin private-catalog.json`
+- `native_shader_index match owned-cache.bin stage snapshot|instructions complete-code.bin private-match.json [required-metadata-sha256]`
+- `native_shader_matched_pair owned-cache.bin complete-vertex-snapshot.bin complete-fragment-snapshot.bin private-output-directory`
+
+The matched-pair tool first proves exact stage/code/environment matches and then runs the existing explicitly conservative CPU translator. It reports queried pixel formats. It does not validate captured vertex/raster state, Vulkan capabilities, pipeline creation or drawing. Ambiguous fragment contexts fail; callers must establish authoritative captured metadata rather than retarget historical handles silently.
+
+Synthetic tests cover SHA256 vectors, all-record traversal, graphics/compute/geometry metadata, explicit instruction layout, malformed count/extent/version/truncated keys, stage/SPH/key mismatch, exact-length and stage rejection, identical aliases, metadata ambiguity/selector, missing metadata and unsupported shifted format queries. Fixtures contain no game code. Actual cache/code/catalog/SPIR-V outputs remain private and must not be committed as source assets.
+
+## Owned native source input (offline tooling)
+
+`Snapshot::FromNativeInput(const NativeInput&)` accepts named `NativeStage::VertexB`
+or `Fragment`, source bytes beginning with the complete 80-byte SPH, and an explicit
+start address. It copies source/header/cbuf/texture/replacement state; callers may
+release or mutate every input buffer after return. The CFG still starts at start+80
+through the same TranslatePair path. The source must contain at least one complete
+8-byte executable word, have an 8-byte aligned start and size, fit the existing
+1MiB+8 bound, and have its final word address fit u32. Input extent completeness
+and provenance remain the caller's responsibility: structural validation is not
+source attestation or proof that every possible branch is captured.
+
+Required metadata uses optionals: local_memory_size (u32-representable),
+viewport_transform (explicit 0 or 1), texture_bound_bank (0..17), and
+proprietary_driver (explicit Boolean). Explicit zero/false differ from absence.
+The bank domain follows Shader::Info::MAX_CBUFS=18 and Maxwell graphics cbuf arrays.
+PositionPass treats zero/nonzero viewport state as disabled/enabled; this factory
+restricts it to the known Boolean domain rather than accepting arbitrary integers.
+Existing GraphicsEnvironment derives proprietary driver iff texture bank==2;
+the factory requires the same consistent pairing. The driver flag enables driver
+constant folding, so it must come from a verified input observation. Local memory
+size is explicit environment metadata, not guessed from a zero default. The SPH is
+copied from the source and its shader-type tag must match the named stage.
+
+Cbuf/replacement keys retain bank and byte offset independently in the existing
+64-bit key. Banks must be below18, offsets aligned4 with offset+4<=65536, and
+replacement enums must be BaseInstance/BaseVertex/DrawID. Texture keys retain the
+full raw u32 handle, including zero and UINT32_MAX. Texture type must belong to the
+nine declared TextureType values. Typed native pixel formats are a deliberately
+small semantic subset (RGBA8 unorm/snorm/sint/uint, BGRA8 unorm, R32 and RGBA32
+float/sint/uint), explicitly switched to Shader::TexturePixelFormat. No Surface
+ordinal cast occurs. Missing optional formats remain missing and fail only if
+queried; formats are never inferred from texture type. Each map and their combined
+record count are capped at65536. Duplicate keys, even identical duplicates, fail.
+All counts/ranges/enums are preflighted before owned storage allocation/copy;
+rejection returns no object and does not modify a prior Snapshot or caller buffers.
+
+Version18 parsing/serialization and raw shifted-format rejection remain intact.
+Required read diagnostics now identify operation and full encoded key. Existing
+inherited translator lookup caches are populated by the translator; the native
+factory does not accept partial bank/offset/handle cache keys or seed these caches.
+
+Build from this directory with the existing matched source/frozen offline library
+kit configured, then build `native_shader_native_input_test` and
+`native_shader_cache_index_test`; run CTest. Native factory translation unit and
+synthetic native input test use MSVC `/W4 /WX /analyze`; third-party includes are
+SYSTEM/external and excluded from their unrelated static-analysis diagnostics.
+The test authors public EXIT-only VertexB/Fragment fixtures, compares all emitted
+SPIR-V/resource-plan bytes to an equivalent authored v18 pair, checks all supported
+semantic format mappings, missing fields vs zero, duplicate/full keys, bank/offset/
+handle/count/extent limits, ownership, failure atomicity and shifted ordinals94/95/
+111/112. Cache-index regressions cover all-record traversal and old schema behavior.
+No private cache or shader bytes are required for these tests.
+
+This is offline translation tooling linked to frozen shader/compiler libraries.
+It is not a final runtime dependency claim, native capture adapter, shader catalog,
+Vulkan module/pipeline acceptance or native rendered frame. TranslatePair retains
+its documented conservative profile/triangle/float specialization assumptions;
+unknown actual draw specialization remains a gate.
