diff --git a/tests/native_pending/README.md b/tests/native_pending/README.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/native_pending/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# Native API v3 pending transport
+
+`run.py --build <private-build-directory>` builds/runs only owned synthetic
+fixtures with at most two compiler jobs. It performs no GPU, game or service work.
+V1/V2 and ordinary runtime caches remain independent. This transport is
+infrastructure evidence, not DeviceInitialize/MemoryPoolInitialize coverage.
+
+`NativePendingDescriptor` pins module build ID, text SHA, canonical entry, complete
+wrapper/body words, operation/signature revision, result kind and a separate
+approved public/provider contract SHA. Unlike v2's closed-CFG rule, v3 explicitly
+models a whole API with verified excluded callees/providers. The host must validate
+that contract and mutable provider identity; the contract hash is not permission
+to skip unknown behavior. Strict mode is the default. Interior entries and unknown
+bindings/operations fail unsupported; original execution is available only when
+the descriptor explicitly selects comparison mode before any admission effects.
+
+Each selected module negotiates `recomp_image_native_pending_v3`. Its monotonically
+changing acknowledgement epoch revokes old admissions on re-negotiation. The
+separate BindingV3 requires exact revision, size, GuestContext size/layout,
+capabilities and reserved halt tag. Binding install/revoke is quiescent and bumps
+an independent epoch. GuestContext layout and pending_svc are unchanged.
+
+The binding callbacks are pure identify/validate, bounded admit, acquire-state
+poll, owner commit and cancellation. Identify supplies stable thread/context
+generation plus a validation epoch. Validate checks actual immutable sealed code,
+provider slots, address space, descriptor and native ownership at admission and
+again before commit. Every covered code range is guarded before effects and
+rechecked before completion. The host record copies required inputs and retains
+module/binding/resources until work actually drains. Worker payloads never retain
+GuestContext pointers or raw guest spans, and owner-only GPU operations cannot run
+on arbitrary workers. No pending job implementation is hidden in the runtime.
+
+Pending preserves API-entry PC, LR/SP, SVC and remaining chain budget, sets only
+the reserved halt and unwinds generated C frames. Completion restores AAPCS state,
+publishes checked outputs, the declared result and saved LR return PC. Bool is
+canonical 0/1; int32/uint32 use zero-extended W0 bits; int64/uint64/guest pointers
+retain all bits; void preserves x0; float32/float64 publish low s0/d0 bits with
+otherwise stronger preservation. x18 through x31, full v8 through v15, FPCR/FPSR
+are preserved. Native calls/jobs/yields/completions/work units are separate from
+actual guest block dispatch. Ready reply work units are reported units, never an
+estimate of skipped basic blocks; the host also accounts private failed/cancelled
+work when draining jobs.
+
+Commit's unchanged integer callback signature carries an explicit tri-state:
+`COMMIT_DONE=1`, `COMMIT_FAILED=0`, `COMMIT_CANCELLED=2`. Accepted cancellation
+before the owner's atomic publication claim returns Cancelled, not generic false.
+Unknown commit values fault. Cancellation requests alone must not be classified as
+identity revocation by pure validation; poll/commit report their actual outcome.
+Tests cover synchronous and pending cancellation at this claim boundary, exact
+terminal tags/counters, and absence of guest output publication.
+
+The build must include v3 support exactly once in its shared runtime. Selecting
+an earlier non-v3 module's runtime as the generic first CMake owner does not
+automatically compose optional helpers from a later module. Explicitly choose
+the v3 runtime owner or compile `NativePendingC` with its matching header into
+the optional host target; negotiate every selected module before dispatch.
+
+Host poll/cancel must pass the LIVE registry's current thread ID, context
+generation and active token as the last three arguments. Passing saved IDs/token
+blindly would defeat reuse protection. Stale completions leave a new context/job
+untouched. Failed/Cancelled use terminal reserved halts; repeated dispatch/poll
+does not repeat the hook, return success, fall back or spin. After terminal
+transport, old worker resources still need host-owned cancellation/draining.
+
+Tests cover nine return kinds, sync/parked completion, direct host entry, local
+BL/BLR and cross-module calls, budgets 0/1/2/8, exact block/native counters,
+immutable snapshots and release/acquire workers, binding/module/provider/seal/
+address-space/descriptor revocation, cancellation phases, partial commit faults,
+late/duplicate completions, thread/context/token reuse, teardown and synthetic
+job failure/deadline states. All 36 wrapper/body words are mutated both before
+admission and before commit in each chain mode. Strict and comparison interiors
+are checked independently.
+
+The current generic Translate path emits ordinary PC+return branches; its
+ChainTo/ChainIndirect helpers have no call sites there. The second fixture mode
+explicitly substitutes those existing helper bodies only in owned generated test
+callers. This proves their call/return unwind without changing legacy exports or
+claiming all production bundles use chaining. Host integration and real provider,
+driver, deadline, sealing and resource-lifetime contracts need their own proofs.
+
+## Selectable native feature profile
+
+Add `--native-profile` to run.py (or as the generator's second argument) for
+FM1/GG1/FPX1, ABI 6, feature mask 7. Use a separate build directory. The default
+remains the original FM0 fixture. Both modules negotiate guard version 2,
+generation version 2, exact fastmem layout and FPX offsets before publishing
+generation 1. Synthetic instruction pages are mapped read-only and watched;
+mutations update the actual mapped bytes and publish a new generation.
+
+The profile-only cache observer retains the real guard macro and checks canonical
+slot zero: first entry misses, same-generation entry hits, and published generation
+2 misses again. Full pending range validation remains active independently.
+These watched, stable synthetic pages are a fixture seal contract, not evidence
+of a sealed actual game module or native Device implementation.
