diff --git a/tests/native_pending_host/README.md b/tests/native_pending_host/README.md
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/native_pending_host/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Emitted CPU pending owner verification
+
+Run `run.py --build BUILD --generated VERIFIED_PENDING_FIXTURES` after the separate `tests/native_pending` transport runner has produced and verified its ordinary and chained fixtures. Builds use the installed CMake/MSVC toolchain, at most two BelowNormal jobs, and no downloaded dependencies.
+
+This target compiles the actual standalone Host dispatcher, sparse address space, optional PendingOwnerV3 bridge, emitted revision-3 module/shared runtime and emitted cross-module caller. It runs synthetic owner jobs only. No GPU operation, driver scheduling, gameplay or performance result is claimed.
+
+The legacy CPU target owns only the type-erased scheduler interface and references no v3 C symbols. The concrete owner is compiled only for a target supplying the optional emitted v3 runtime. GuestContext and RecompHostMem layouts remain those of the selected emitted ABI. The module must negotiate v3 separately; binding does not replace per-module negotiation.
+
+Tests cover exact entered-block accounting across canonical/direct BL/BLR/cross-module entries and budgets1/2/4096, parked/exhausted budgets, complete context AAPCS restoration, interruption, immutable copied input, owner-only commit, release/acquire completion publication, concurrent cancel/publication, repeated terminal dispatch, provider/resource/descriptor/address-space/binding/module-generation revocation, retirement/reuse, duplicate/late completion and retained teardown tickets. Completion tickets retain immutable input/resource ownership and contain no Host or GuestContext pointer. Context generations and operation tokens are process-monotonic and never recycled.
+
+The initial scheduler executes bounded work on its context owner after all generated C frames have unwound. External completion publication can only update a retained record; it cannot commit guest state. A future asynchronous backend must retain the ticket and its input ownership until work/fences have finished. GPU-affine resource destruction and a concurrent application scheduler remain separate work. Validation and snapshot providers must remain bounded and effect-free; commit failures are terminal and never resume the original API body.
+
+Compiled fixture modules and their descriptor/epoch storage have process lifetime; this host exposes no module unload path. One owner binds each shared runtime at a time. The owner diagnostic work-unit counter counts the first completion report even when cancellation discards it; the emitted transport counter separately counts accepted reply-reported units. Neither substitutes native work units for guest blocks.
+
+Completion polling snapshots state and result under the publication mutex. Commit claims publication under that same mutex before calling the provider outside the lock. Cancellation accepted before this claim prevents guest commit and reports the explicit Cancelled outcome; cancellation after the claim returns false. Retirement and teardown notify the provider once on its owner and retain old input/resource tickets until they drain.
+
+The same owner suite also runs against the emitted native profile (ABI6/features7, FM1+GG1+FPX1) by selecting `native-pending-native-profile/generated` with `--generated` and a separate `--build` directory. Both target and caller negotiate exact fastmem offsets/mask, guard generation and FPX offsets/inhibit. The Host uses authoritative memory callbacks and immutable sealed code; this proves the production context layout and transport without claiming a raw-fastmem or graphics backend. Profile assertions require genuine first-entry verification and no guest reentry while parked. The FM0 fixture remains a separate regression.
